  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "32e30ab9-4ec7-4e3d-8054-38190fcdcd6a",
    "name": "Tackle Public Contracts Authentication API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "Customer-facing read API for cloud marketplace contracts that Tackle has\ningested for your Tackle account.\n\nThe response shape is a stable projection of the underlying\ncontract document. It is intended to be safe to consume long-term: fields\nwill be added over time, but documented fields will not be removed without\ndeprecation notice.\n\n## Authentication\n\nEvery request must include a valid Tackle JWT in the `Authorization`\nheader (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`). Machine-to-machine (MTM) tokens\nissued for your Tackle account are accepted. The token scopes every\nresponse to the account it represents.\n\n## Pagination\n\n`GET /api/contracts` is the only paginated endpoint. Pagination uses an\nopaque `cursor` query parameter:\n\n1. The first request omits `cursor`.\n2. If more pages exist, the response includes a `next` field. Pass that\n   value verbatim back as `cursor` on the next request.\n3. The last page omits `next`.\n\nCursors are opaque tokens. Do not parse, modify, or persist them across\nschema changes — request a fresh page from the start instead.\n",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
